<statement>
<p>
Solve the following linear system.  If the system has an infinite number of solutions, parameterize the solution set in terms of the free variables of the original system.</p>
<p>
<m>\displaystyle{\left\lbrace\begin{array}{ccccccccc} {3}{x}\amp-\amp{y}\amp-\amp{5}{z}\amp+\amp{26}{w}\amp=\amp-{57}\\-{7}{x}\amp-\amp{9}{y}\amp-\amp{8}{z}\amp+\amp{120}{w}\amp=\amp-{81}\\-{3}{x}\amp-\amp{4}{y}\amp-\amp{6}{z}\amp+\amp{63}{w}\amp=\amp-{56}\end{array}\right.}</m></p>
<p>
x = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
y = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
z = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
w = <fillin characters="20"/>  

</p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li><m>\displaystyle-{4}+{1}{w}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{5}+{9}{w}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{8}+{4}{w}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{w}</m></li></ul></p>
</answer>

